{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1121618-creating-a-brood-representing-it-in-game","id":1121618,"title":"Creating a Brood, Representing it in game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-27T16:47:59-07:00","id":1121618,"title":"Creating a Brood, Representing it in game?","content":"So, if my party is convinced to re-roll and play the system properly we'll be playing base + 10xp.<br /> <br /> Anyway, my first thought was just give them all 2 dots of Allies: Brood and call it a day, build as normal - is that the usual method or do people have a better means of handling &quot;Allies&quot;/&quot;Family&quot;?<br /> <br /> Do various groups do it differently? If so, how?<br /> <br /> What's your take on the whole Brood/Family thing and how it can be represented (and role played) in game. I'm likely the only beast (maybe one other?) among vampires, likely mages so naturally I'm spinning the wheels in dead water until everyone's ready to game again.<br /> <br /> Also, on a somewhat unrelated note, the brood I've made summarized.<br /> <br /> Reindal - PC, Eshmaki Spear Hunter. Fenris inspired by Hell. Physical &gt; Mental &gt; Social, the group's skirmisher.<br /> Soralia - Ugallu Bow Hunter. Raven that only. Physical &gt; Mental &gt; Social. Seeker and support of the brood.<br /> Tyrs - Anakim who likes seeing how people tick. Likes to act in charge. Perfectly symmetric &quot;porcelain&quot; angel. Physical &gt; Social &gt; Mental<br /> Anasra - Makara, morbid &quot;cultist-ish&quot; Eccentric but mostly harmless. Looming Serpent horror. Social &gt; Mental &gt; Physical","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 07-27-2017, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T18:42:39-07:00","id":1121659,"title":"","content":"Is this a Dark Eras game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T04:33:10-07:00","id":1121782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1121618-creating-a-brood-representing-it-in-game?p=1121659#post1121659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this a Dark Eras game?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Just Beast, probably VtR2 maybe MtA2. Just trying to represent a family in game without having to play 5 characters instead of 1 (hence dots of Allies all representing each other, for the quick and simple stuff)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T06:22:01-07:00","id":1121801,"title":"","content":"So, you are playing a Beast with his own Brood? Why not just be a Beast with a non-Beast Brood and be a family with the other players?<br /> <br /> Anywho, depending on the Power of your Brood, I'd go with 3-4 dots.<br /> A Brood is rather closely and intimately connected, much more so than most other splats are thanks to their shared Brood Lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T08:45:28-07:00","id":1121880,"title":"","content":"Our group tends to play for power with suspicion. Figured it might pay to start with a few members since it could be a while before I get an ally in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value"